a Go runtime OOM, exit 2 and no envelope\n114:- **Severity:** CRIT\n115:- **File:** internal/gen/gen.go:178\n130:## Finding 8: Every history append rewrites the whole store under the cross-process lock, costing seconds and gigabytes per call\n132:- **Severity:** CRIT\n133:- **File:** internal/corpus/store.go:99\n146:## Finding 9: SIGINT and SIGTERM are swallowed for the process lifetime, and the curl version preflight is unbounded\n148:- **Severity:** WARN\n149:- **File:** cmd/talaria/root.go:207\n153:## Finding 10: A credential in a path parameter is never redacted — cleartext on stdout, in the emitted curl, and in history\n155:- **Severity:** WARN\n156:- **File:** internal/request/build.go:225\n169:## Finding 11: `run --fail-on-error` exits 0 on a suite where every operation was skipped\n171:- **Severity:** WARN\n172:- **File:** cmd/talaria/run.go:450\n184:## Finding 12: Emitted curl for an inline sensitive header silently reproduces a *different* request\n186:- **Severity:** WARN\n187:- **File:** internal/curl/render.go:224\n199:## Finding 13: A spec's credential header name is not held to the HTTP field-name charset\n201:- **Severity:** WARN\n202:- **File:** internal/request/build.go:500\n212:## Finding 14: JUnit and JSON reports show 0 ms for any operation that timed out or failed to connect\n214:- **Severity:** WARN\n215:- **File:** cmd/talaria/run.go:415\n228:## Finding 15: Warnings on stderr are plain text, breaking the documented \"stderr is JSON\" contract\n230:- **Severity:** WARN\n231:- **File:** internal/secret/response.go:260\n245:## Finding 16: `valid_alternatives` is capped at 5, but AGENT.md tells the agent it is the complete set\n247:- **Severity:** WARN\n248:- **File:** internal/operation/index.go:16\n260:## Finding 17: `call --output pretty` — the TTY default — never shows the response body\n262:- **Severity:** WARN\n263:- **File:** cmd/talaria/call.go:475\n276:## Finding 18: The §5a canary gate has no case for a validation-error path — the one error path the doc names explicitly\n278:- **Severity:** WARN\n279:- **File:** internal/canary/canary_test.go:427\n283:## Finding 19: No canary mechanism drives a profile-supplied credential, the second of the two auth sources §5 defines\n285:- **Severity:** WARN\n286:- **File:** internal/canary/canary_test.go:99\n290:## Finding 20: Swagger 2.0 \"conversion fidelity against real 2.0 specs\" is verified only against 3-operation miniatures\n292:- **Severity:** WARN\n293:- **File:** internal/spec/convert_test.go:87\n304:## Finding 21: The history store is never fsynced, so a crash can lose the whole file rather than one entry\n306:- **Severity:** WARN\n307:- **File:** internal/corpus/store.go:298\n311:## Finding 22: A kill during `trim` leaks a full-store-sized temp file that nothing ever removes\n313:- **Severity:** WARN\n314:- **File:** internal/corpus/store.go:301\n324:## Finding 23: The process-group kill has no already-reaped guard\n326:- **Severity:** WARN\n327:- **File:** internal/curl/procgroup_unix.go:33\n331:## Finding 24: The non-unix corpus lock is a silent no-op\n333:- **Severity:** WARN\n334:- **File:** internal/corpus/lock_other.go:11\n338:## Finding 25: `--output tsv` silently renders `pretty` on `describe`, `call` and `history show`\n340:- **Severity:** INFO\n341:- **File:** internal/output/render.go:105\n352:## Finding 26: `--timeout` above ~9.2e9 seconds silently reverts to the 30 s default\n354:- **Severity:** INFO\n355:- **File:** cmd/talaria/call.go:230\n359:## Finding 27: `run`'s missing-credential message is ungrammatical\n361:- **Severity:** INFO\n362:- **File:** cmd/talaria/run.go:447",
