ets on disk: file modes on the profile config, history store, temp files. Any credential written to history or corpus.\n- Resource exhaustion on untrusted input: a hostile OpenAPI spec or a hostile history/corpus file causing OOM, panic, or hang.\n- Any credential, key, or token literal committed in the diff.\n- Env var namespace: DESIGN.md restricts resolvable env vars to `TALARIA_AUTH_*`. Verify no path escapes that namespace.\n\nRULES:\n- Every finding MUST have a real `file.go:LINE` reference that you verified by reading the file. No guesses.\n- Report only issues in code on this branch, not hypotheticals about unwritten future phases.\n- Severity CRIT means \"must not ship\": a credential reaching a forbidden surface, data loss/corruption, crash/hang on untrusted input, silently wrong results, or violation of an explicit DESIGN.md contract. Everything else is WARN. Style/docs are INFO. Do not inflate.\n- For each finding also decide: is it fixable within the design as written (`Blocked-by: none`), or does a fix require inventing a policy the design doc never states (`Blocked-by: design`)? If design-blocked, state exactly which decision is missing.\n\nReturn your findings as a numbered list. For each: Title, Severity (CRIT/WARN/INFO), Blocked-by (none|design), File:line, Description (what is wrong and why it matters), Suggested fix (concrete). Be rigorous and concise. Do not write any files."
