oroughly they would not catch a real breakage.\n6. The canary CI suite (internal/canary/, internal/ci/workflow_test.go, .github/workflows/ci.yml): DESIGN.md §5a mandates a suite that injects canary secrets through EVERY auth mechanism and greps EVERY output surface (json, pretty, tsv, dry-run, errors, junit reports, history store, corpus files, debug logs). Verify the suite actually covers every mechanism and every surface named, and that CI actually runs it and fails the build on a leak. Gaps here are real findings.\n7. internal/e2e/: do the end-to-end tests exercise the real binary and real curl, or do they shortcut?\n\nRULES:\n- Every finding MUST have a real `file.go:LINE` (or ci.yml:LINE) you verified by reading the file. No guesses.\n- CRIT = must not ship: silently wrong results the caller cannot detect, data loss, a broken contract DESIGN.md states explicitly, or a leaked secret. Missing test coverage is normally WARN. Do not inflate.\n- For each finding decide `Blocked-by: none` or `Blocked-by: design` (fix requires a policy decision the doc never makes — state it).\n- Only report code on this branch.\n\nReturn a numbered list: Title, Severity (CRIT/WARN/INFO), Blocked-by, File:line, Description, Suggested fix. Be rigorous and concise. Do not write any files."
