    "content": [
      {
        "tool_use_id": "toolu_017tNRit97AXCoSdYQfUCc9Q",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "1\tpackage curl\n2\t\n3\timport (\n4\t\t\"os\"\n5\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n6\t\t\"strings\"\n7\t\t\"time\"\n8\t)\n9\t\n10\t// The prefixes talaria gives its own temp files, matching what newCapture and\n11\t// document.tempFile pass to the os package. They are the only names the sweep\n12\t// will remove: everything else in TMPDIR belongs to somebody else.\n13\tconst (\n14\t\tcapturePrefix = \"talaria-call-\"\n15\t\tbodyPrefix    = \"talaria-body-\"\n16\t)\n17\t\n18\t// staleGrace is how old one of talaria's temp files has to be before the sweep\n19\t// takes it.\n20\t//\n21\t// A day is far longer than any request: the default max-time is 30s and even a\n22\t// generous --timeout is minutes. The margin is deliberate, because the cost of\n23\t// the two errors is not symmetric — sweeping a live call's capture out from\n24\t// under it breaks a request that was working, while leaving a dead one an extra\n25\t// hour costs nothing that the SIGKILL had not already cost.\n26\tconst staleGrace = 24 * time.Hour\n27\t\n28\t// SweepStale removes talaria's own leftover temp files from TMPDIR.\n29\t//\n30\t// It is the backstop for SIGKILL, the one signal no handler can catch: cleanup\n31\t// there cannot run at all, so a capture directory holding the *raw, unredacted*\n32\t// response — and the request body, which may carry a credential the user put in\n33\t// it — would otherwise sit in TMPDIR until the machine was rebooted. Every\n34\t// other way of dying is handled by the context reaching curl and the defers\n35\t// running.\n36\t//\n37\t// It is silent and best-effort by design. Nobody ran talaria to have their temp\n38\t// directory tidied, so a permission error on somebody else's file, or a TMPDIR\n39\t// that cannot be read at all, is not worth a word on stderr.\n40\tfunc SweepStale() {\n41\t\tdir := os.TempDir()\n42\t\n43\t\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(dir)\n44\t\tif err != nil {\n45\t\t\treturn\n46\t\t}\n47\t\n48\t\tcutoff := time.Now().Add(-staleGrace)\n49\t\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n50\t\t\tname := entry.Name()\n51\t\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(name, capturePrefix) && !strings.HasPrefix(name, bodyPrefix) {\n52\t\t\t\tcontinue\n53\t\t\t}\n54\t\n55\t\t\t// Info is lstat here, so a symlink somebody planted under one of these\n56\t\t\t// names is judged and removed as the link it is, never followed.\n57\t\t\tinfo, err := entry.Info()\n58\t\t\tif err != nil || !info.ModTime().Before(cutoff) {\n59\t\t\t\tcontinue\n60\t\t\t}\n61\t\n62\t\t\tos.RemoveAll(filepath.Join(dir, name)) //nolint:errcheck // Best effort.\n63\t\t}\n64\t}\n65\t"
      }
