        "content": "AGENT.md:9:your context is not a supported workflow — see [Credentials](#credentials) for what to do instead.\nAGENT.md:43:| `talaria history [--operation id] [--since 1h] [--status 4xx] [--source call\\|run\\|replay]` | what has already been called |\nAGENT.md:45:| `talaria history replay <id\\|n>` | send a recorded request again |\nAGENT.md:62:- `--base-url` overrides the spec's server. `--profile` selects a named profile from the user's\nAGENT.md:106:to exercise a `DELETE` is against a disposable environment — point `--base-url` at one. (The\nAGENT.md:114:talaria run ./openapi.yaml --tag pets --operation getPet --base-url http://localhost:9000\nAGENT.md:197:Response bodies are redacted only at the OAuth2 token fields and whatever JSON paths the user\nAGENT.md:220:| 1 | The request could not be completed: network, TLS, curl itself | check the host and `--base-url`; retrying once is reasonable |\nAGENT.md:236:Each entry has an `id` and an index, and `show` and `replay` take either. **Use the id.** The\nAGENT.md:238:anything is recorded — and `call`, `run` and `replay` all record, replay included. Two replays in\nAGENT.md:243:`talaria history replay <id|n>` re-sends an entry and records the result as a new one;\nAGENT.md:244:replaying a mutation needs `--allow-mutations` too. Dry runs are never recorded. Recording is off\nAGENT.md:248:Credentials are stored as names, so nothing in history can be read back into a value. On replay\nREADME.md:165:API keys are supported in all three locations — `header`, `query` and `cookie`. OAuth2 and\nREADME.md:168:one it can supply *and* has every credential for, so a spec offering \"OAuth2 or a bearer token\"\nREADME.md:170:you exported. When no alternative is fully covered, the first supported one is named in the\nREADME.md:174:with `--profile`. `--profile` and `--base-url` are accepted by every command that makes\nREADME.md:180:    base-url: https://staging.example.com\nREADME.md:192:from every source, including a stored history entry on the way to a replay. A base URL is copied\nREADME.md:254:talaria cannot supply at all (OAuth2, OpenID Connect) are left out rather than reported missing.\nREADME.md:304:response *bodies* are redacted only at the JSON paths you configure, plus the OAuth2 token\nREADME.md:375:talaria history replay 3\nREADME.md:381:or `replay` — so a smoke run over a large spec does not bury the calls you made by hand. The\nREADME.md:383:renumber it — but a *write* does, and `call`, `run` and `replay` all write. The id is the handle\nREADME.md:384:that does not move: it is assigned once, at record time, and both `show` and `replay` prefer it\nREADME.md:387:`history show <id|n>` prints one entry in full; `history replay <id|n>` sends it again and records\nREADME.md:388:the result as a new entry, leaving the original alone. Replay resolves credentials from the\nREADME.md:390:in the file to read back. It is gated the same way `call` is: replaying a `POST` needs\nREADME.md:392:reproduced, and replay says so on stderr rather than pretending it sent one.\nREADME.md:394:The names replay will resolve are an allowlist, not whatever the file asks for: `TALARIA_AUTH_BEARER`,\nREADME.md:396:map names. That is exactly the set talaria records, so a normal replay is unaffected — but the store\nREADME.md:397:is a plain file, and an entry edited to name some other variable would otherwise make replay a way to\nREADME.md:408:and a replay would send something the original call did not; `history show` reports such a body\nREADME.md:438:talaria run ./openapi.yaml --base-url http://localhost:9000\nREADME.md:474:talaria run ./openapi.yaml --base-url \"$STAGING\" --report junit > report.xml",
