    "prompt": "You are the SPEC-COMPLIANCE reviewer for a code review of the Go CLI project at /home/casper/projects/talaria, branch `ralph/design` vs base `main`.\n\nThe entire implementation is new on this branch, so treat all of `cmd/` and `internal/` as in-scope. File list:\n  git -C /home/casper/projects/talaria diff --stat main...HEAD -- cmd internal\n\nTHE SPEC IS docs/design/DESIGN.md (v0.4). Read it in full. Also read AGENT.md and README.md — README.md and AGENT.md are shipped documentation, so code contradicting them is drift too.\n\nThe design was just amended to v0.4 (commit 58af63c) adding three invariants; also read docs/design/proposals/2026-08-03-amendments.md. The three:\n  (a) §5a \"Credentials bind to hosts\" — allowed host set = spec servers[] + `--allow-host` + profile `allow_hosts`; off-set `--base-url` runs WITHOUT credentials and reports `credentials_withheld` in the envelope + a stderr warning; `auth check` reports against the resolved host set.\n  (b) §5a \"History is untrusted input when read\" — `history replay` re-derives operationId/params/body/credentials/target host rather than trusting stored fields; stored host outside the allowed set = exit 2; only `TALARIA_AUTH_*` env names resolvable; sizes/types bounded so a corrupt entry fails that entry, not the process.\n  (c) §5 — a security scheme v1 cannot resolve (oauth2/openIdConnect/mutualTLS) is UNSUPPORTED, NOT INVISIBLE: satisfied by `TALARIA_AUTH_BEARER` if set, otherwise `auth check` reports `{\"scheme\":\"oauth2\",\"supported\":false,\"present\":false}` and exits 5, and call/run exit 5 naming the scheme and the variable.\n\nI have already confirmed (a) is entirely unimplemented (no --allow-host, no allow_hosts, no credentials_withheld in any .go file) — do NOT re-verify or report that; I will report it. DO carefully verify (b) and (c) against the actual code in cmd/talaria/history.go, cmd/talaria/auth.go, internal/config/auth.go, cmd/talaria/call.go and cmd/talaria/run.go, since those are partially implemented and the details matter.\n\nThen check the rest of the spec:\n- Completeness: is every CLI flag and command in §4 implemented with the documented behaviour? (list/describe/search/uses/call/history/run/auth check/version; flags like --param/--query/--header/--body/--base-url/--profile/--dry-run/--allow-mutations/--timeout/--output/--report/--fail-on-error/--fixtures)\n- Exit codes §4 table: 0/1/2/3/4/5 — verify each is produced where documented.\n- Output contract: `\"schema\": \"talaria/v1\"`, the `call` envelope shape in §4, `validation` block, errors to stderr as structured JSON with \"valid alternatives\".\n- §5a leak-channel table: is each countermeasure actually implemented?\n- §5a test-data priority order for `run`: spec example/examples → fixture files → gen.\n- §3 principles: never prompt, never page, no interactivity; pretty-on-TTY / JSON-when-piped default; curl >= 7.70 version floor check; `--dry-run` prints exact curl and exits 0.\n- Drift: anything in the code contradicting the doc or README without a recorded reason.\n- Scope creep: anything implemented from Phases 5-8 (twin, recording proxy) that shouldn't be here yet is worth a note, not a CRIT.\n\nRULES:\n- Every finding MUST have a real `file.go:LINE` you verified by reading the file. No guesses.\n- CRIT = must not ship: violation of a contract DESIGN.md or shipped docs explicitly state, silently wrong results, data loss, crash on untrusted input. Missing feature that merely degrades = WARN. Do not inflate WARN to CRIT.\n- For each finding decide `Blocked-by: none` (fixable within the design as written) or `Blocked-by: design` (fix requires a policy decision the doc never makes — state the missing decision explicitly).\n\nReturn a numbered list: Title, Severity, Blocked-by, File:line, Description, Suggested fix. Be rigorous and concise. Do not write any files.",
