    "prompt": "You are the SECURITY reviewer for a code review of the Go CLI project at /home/casper/projects/talaria, branch `ralph/design` vs base `main`.\n\nThe entire implementation is new on this branch, so treat all of `cmd/` and `internal/` as in-scope diff. Get the file list with:\n  git -C /home/casper/projects/talaria diff --stat main...HEAD -- cmd internal\n\nREAD FIRST (mandatory): docs/design/DESIGN.md — especially §3 principle 0, §5 (Auth), and §5a (The credential firewall). This project's ENTIRE reason to exist is a credential firewall: \"no consumer of stdout or stderr ever observes a credential value\". Also read AGENT.md and README.md for documented contracts.\n\nDesign v0.4 (2026-08-03) added three NEW invariants in §5/§5a. I have already confirmed the first is completely unimplemented (no `--allow-host` flag, no `allow_hosts` profile key, no `credentials_withheld` envelope field anywhere in the Go source) — you do NOT need to re-verify that one; I will report it myself. Focus your effort elsewhere.\n\nYour checklist:\n- Injection: command/argv construction in internal/curl (config document escaping in internal/curl/config.go is high risk — can a header value, body, or credential name break out of the `-K -` config document syntax and inject a new curl directive? Check quoting/escaping of `\"`, `\\`, newlines, and how `data`/`header` directives are written).\n- Output escaping / redaction completeness: internal/secret/redact.go, internal/secret/response.go, internal/output/*. Does every output surface (json, pretty, tsv, junit, dry-run curl, error messages, history store) go through redaction? Look for a path that formats a raw Request rather than the redacted representation.\n- Path traversal: spec loading from file/URL (internal/spec/source.go), `--body @file`, fixture dirs (internal/gen/fixtures.go), corpus/history file paths, the temp-file fallback for large bodies (§5a says 0600 and deleted immediately after exec — verify both).\n- Secrets on disk: file modes on the profile config, history store, temp files. Any credential written to history or corpus.\n- Resource exhaustion on untrusted input: a hostile OpenAPI spec or a hostile history/corpus file causing OOM, panic, or hang.\n- Any credential, key, or token literal committed in the diff.\n- Env var namespace: DESIGN.md restricts resolvable env vars to `TALARIA_AUTH_*`. Verify no path escapes that namespace.\n\nRULES:\n- Every finding MUST have a real `file.go:LINE` reference that you verified by reading the file. No guesses.\n- Report only issues in code on this branch, not hypotheticals about unwritten future phases.\n- Severity CRIT means \"must not ship\": a credential reaching a forbidden surface, data loss/corruption, crash/hang on untrusted input, silently wrong results, or violation of an explicit DESIGN.md contract. Everything else is WARN. Style/docs are INFO. Do not inflate.\n- For each finding also decide: is it fixable within the design as written (`Blocked-by: none`), or does a fix require inventing a policy the design doc never states (`Blocked-by: design`)? If design-blocked, state exactly which decision is missing.\n\nReturn your findings as a numbered list. For each: Title, Severity (CRIT/WARN/INFO), Blocked-by (none|design), File:line, Description (what is wrong and why it matters), Suggested fix (concrete). Be rigorous and concise. Do not write any files.",
