  "result": "**32 findings — 8 CRIT, 17 WARN, 7 INFO.** Committed as `e577993`.\n\n## Context that shapes this cycle\n\nNo code has changed since the last review (`ddb5e6a`). That cycle ended in a **design amendment** (v0.4) rather than a fix pass, and its findings file was deliberately cleared. So most repeats here are *unattempted*, not *failed* fixes — I marked them `Repeat-of: none` and said why in the header, since `Repeat-of` is meant to escalate a failed fix approach to a human. Marking six findings as repeats would have escalated the whole cycle for no reason.\n\n**One genuine repeat: Finding 2.** Commit `383eb98` \"restrict history replay to credentials inside the auth namespace\" fixed *which* env var a stored entry may resolve and left *where the resolved value gets sent* untouched. `cmd/talaria/history.go:578` still reads the target host off the JSONL file. That is the partial-fix pattern the review guidance calls out by name.\n\n## The v0.4 invariants land as unblocked work\n\nv0.4 supplied exactly the policy the previous cycle lacked, which converts the recurring design-blocked findings into ordinary fixes:\n\n- **§5a host binding is 100% absent** — `grep` for `credentials_withheld|allow-host|allow_hosts` over all `.go` returns zero hits. A reviewer confirmed on the wire that `--base-url http://127.0.0.1:8765` delivers `Authorization: Bearer SUPERSECRET` to an off-spec host, exit 0, no warning. (Finding 1)\n- **§5a replay re-derivation** is unimplemented in both halves — target host (2) and request reconstruction (3).\n- **§5 unsupported schemes** — `auth check` exits 0 reporting nothing, `call` exits 2, `run` skips and exits 0, all on the same oauth2 spec, with `TALARIA_AUTH_BEARER` set and ignored. (4)\n\n## Two CRITs that are new this cycle\n\n- **Finding 5** — `internal/curl/config.go:290` is the one header path that skips `checkSplit`. A spec `content:` key of `\"application/json\\r\\nX-Injected: pwned\"` was verified to reach the wire as two headers, inside the component that holds resolved credentials. `run` escapes it only by accident.\n- **Finding 6** — a request body is redacted in history but printed cleartext on stdout. The code's own comment at `call.go:303` states the rule this breaks: *\"A pattern that hides a value in the permanent artifact but not on the stdout an agent reads has the firewall backwards.\"* The canary suite does not catch it.\n\nTwo findings are **`Blocked-by: design`** and need a human decision, not code: **18** (DESIGN §5a says replay resolves only `TALARIA_AUTH_*`, while §5/AGENT.md/README all permit profile-referenced variables — two shipped docs contradict each other) and **25** (spec cache has no stated TTL or invalidation policy).\n\nEvery reference was verified against the source before writing. I also recorded a \"Verified clean\" section so the next cycle doesn't re-derive the subprocess lifecycle, locking, and `-K -` mechanism analysis — those are well-built and came back clean.",
